# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What this repo tracks: everything needed to rebuild this project on a fresh
# machine -- the adapter, the experiment scripts, the orchestration drivers in
# scripts/, the AdversariaLLM patches, the chat templates, SETUP.md, the paper
# assets, the working notes, and (since 2026-09-13) the raw results.
#
# results/ and results_*/ are tracked now, the machine that made them is going
# away and the paper figures and tables cant be rebuilt without them. its ~48MB
# of json and png, no single file over 20MB. see the negation rules at the bottom.
#
# What it still does not track: run_logs/ (99MB of console output, nothing reads
# it back) and the run-state markers, which only mean anything on the machine
# that produced them.
#
# The three dependency repos (Balcony-LLaMA, TAO-Attack, AdversariaLLM) are git
# SUBMODULES pinned by commit -- see .gitmodules. AdversariaLLM needs the two
# patches in patches/ applied on top of its pinned commit; nothing else does.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- python -------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
*.egg-info/

# ---- model weights and other large binaries ------------------------------
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.h5
*.pkl

# ---- environment and secrets ---------------------------------------------
.env
*.key
*.pem

# ---- OS and editor junk --------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ---- run bookkeeping -----------------------------------------------------
# Per-shard logs and the .done/.failed/.running/.skipped markers used for
# resume. Machine-local by definition.
run_logs/
run_state/
run_state_*/
*.log
*.log.attempt[0-9]

# ---- build artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
# Rebuild with scripts/make_cluster_bundle.sh.
tao_cluster_bundle.tar.gz

# ---- scratch, backups, superseded archives -------------------------------
.edit_backups/
archive_tao_prefix_*/
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.attempt[0-9]

# ---- json ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Most .json here is run output. The exceptions are source: the adapter's model
# config, and the four small tables the depth figure is rebuilt from.
*.json
!adapter/**/*.json
!experiments/depth_artifact/*.json

# ---- raw results (tracked on purpose) ------------------------------------
# per-behaviour attack records, completions, judge scores and the per-arm
# figures. these come last so they win over *.json and *.bak-* above, the .bak
# files are the pre-nanfix copies and worth keeping.
!results/**
!results_*/**
